
Compile/Build 
=============

1) Compiling under Linux
------------------------
$ autoreconf -i
$ ./configure
$ make


2) Cross-Compiling under Linux, for Windows
-------------------------------------------
$ ./configure  --host=i586-pc-mingw32
(or, to use static linking, which does not require installing any mingw dll's on windows)
$ ./configure  --host=i586-pc-mingw32 LDFLAGS="-static"
$ make





3) Cross-Compiling for Windows with Docker
------------------------------------------
Builds a static 32-bit iec2c.exe into ./dist/. Run from the matiec root.

PowerShell : docker build -t matiec-mingw docker; docker run --rm -v "${PWD}:/src" -v "${PWD}/dist:/out" matiec-mingw
Linux/macOS: docker build -t matiec-mingw docker && docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/src" -v "$PWD/dist:/out" matiec-mingw
Git Bash   : as Linux, but prefix the 'docker run' with MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1

The image build is only needed once. Sources are copied into the container and
built there, so this never touches your working tree except for ./dist/ --
safe to re-run any time, from any state.

4) Native Linux build with Docker
----------------------------------
Builds iec2c into ./dist/, in the same image as (3), same copy-then-build
approach. Run from the matiec root.

PowerShell : docker run --rm -v "${PWD}:/src" -w /src --entrypoint sh matiec-mingw /src/docker/build-native.sh
Git Bash   : MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1 docker run --rm -v "$(pwd -W):/src" -w /src --entrypoint sh matiec-mingw /src/docker/build-native.sh

The bounded-string fixtures are run the same way:
  ... --entrypoint sh matiec-mingw /src/tests/string_widths/run.sh


5) Both binaries in one command (Windows PowerShell)
-----------------------------------------------------
Rebuilds from scratch every time -- safe to re-run unconditionally.

docker build -t matiec-mingw docker; if ($?) { docker run --rm -v "${PWD}:/src" -v "${PWD}/dist:/out" matiec-mingw }; if ($?) { docker run --rm -v "${PWD}:/src" -w /src --entrypoint sh matiec-mingw /src/docker/build-native.sh }

Produces dist\iec2c.exe and dist\iec2c.


Releasing
=========
-> Bump the version reported by `iec2c -v` / `iec2iec -v`: edit the top-level
   VERSION file (e.g. 0.1-alexiii.1 -> 0.1-alexiii.2).


Maintaining the Build Environment
=================================
-> Add new files to Makefile.am or add a new makefile
$ autoreconf


-> Prepare clean project
$ make distclean



-> Remember to add these files to your .hgignore
	Makefile
	config.*
	*.a
	.deps


